cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file.
title: "SHALSTAB: Shallow Landsliding STABility model"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Gómez"
    given-names: "Federico"
    email: "fjgomezc@eafit.edu.co"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8525-4354"
    affiliation: "SIATA, Sistema de Alerta Temprana de Antioquia; Universidad EAFIT"
version: "1.0.3"
date-released: "2025-06-20"
license: GPL-3.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/federicogmz/shalstab-python"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/shalstab/"
abstract: >-
  Python package implementing the SHALSTAB physically-based shallow landslide
  stability model. It combines infinite slope stability analysis, steady-state
  hydrology, and topographic analysis over rasters to map critical rainfall and
  classify slope stability, including the empirical soil thickness model of
  Catani et al. (2010). Developed for rainfall-triggered landslide assessment
  and early warning.
keywords:
  - "landslides"
  - "slope stability"
  - "SHALSTAB"
  - "geohazards"
  - "geomorphology"
  - "rainfall thresholds"
  - "physically-based model"
  - "GIS"
  - "geospatial"
